                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": " Of these choices, fluorine is the strongest oxidizing agent as identified by fluorine having the highest reduction potential because of its strong tendency to gain electrons. Nonmetal elements tend to be oxidizing agents because they tend to gain electrons from another chemical species (increasing the oxidation number of those species), and metal elements tend to be reducing agents because they tend to lose electrons to another chemical species (reducing the oxidation number of those species). "
                  }
                ],
                "id": "wyoowj3i4ey0dbn",
                "type": "p"
              }
            ],
