            },
            {
              "feedback": {
                "content": [
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "text": "Incorrect. Oxidizing agents gain electrons from another chemical species, which means the oxidizing agent is reduced (gain of electrons, decrease in oxidation number) and the other chemical species is oxidized (loss of electrons, increase in oxidation number). Strong oxidizing agents, therefore, have a high potential for being reduced, i.e., a high reduction potential."
                      }
                    ],
                    "id": "jxrmyprw6s2ohf9",
                    "type": "p"
                  },
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "text": " Reducing agents lose electrons to another chemical species, which means the reducing agent is oxidized (loss of electrons, increase in oxidation number) and the other chemical species is reduced (gain of electrons, decrease in oxidation number). Strong reducing agents, therefore, have a high potential for being oxidized, which is the same as a low potential for being reduced, i.e., a low reduction potential."
                      }
                    ],
                    "id": "woe6imvxzqpfxw0",
                    "type": "p"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "680938494"
